# A case where guff writes different bytes than golangci-lint into the same
# lines, on purpose.
#
# Hand-written. Nothing in regen.sh creates a file here. Unlike the other two
# entries, guff does not touch a single line upstream leaves alone: it removes
# exactly what upstream removes and puts something else back. One hunk of the
# 503, everything else is byte-identical.
#
# upstream-writes: 503 line(s), sha256:be06e779bb532ba7
#
# why: golangci-lint's QF1004 rewrites a renamed import's call to the package's
# real name and adds no import, so the replacement names a package that is not
# bound in the file:
#
#     import ( s "strings" )
#     func renamed() { s.Replace("", "", "", -1) }
#
# upstream writes `strings.ReplaceAll("", "", "")` there, which does not
# compile. guff writes `s.ReplaceAll("", "", "")`, which does. That single hunk
# is why `staticcheck-qf` still builds after `guff --fix` and would not after
# upstream's, and it is the reason compat/fix/README.md has said since
# 2026-08-25 that closing it would be a regression: matching upstream here
# means `--fix` starts breaking user builds. A defect upstream ships is not a
# specification — the same call as the `revive` entry.
#
# It sat in pending/ until 2026-08-27 because the case had two real gaps
# alongside it and pending was the only slot that could hold all three. QF1005
# closed those (COMPAT-HARDENING 続き 73), so what is left is this one decision
# and it belongs where decisions are written down.
#
# Fails if guff's bytes move, and fails if upstream's own output moves — if
# QF1004 ever learns to add the import, the digest above stops matching and
# this file has to be read again rather than quietly kept.
--- a/qf1002/bad/bad.go
+++ b/qf1002/bad/bad.go
@@ -4,18 +4,18 @@
 	var x, y int
 	var a bool
 
-	switch {
-	case x == 4:
-	case x == 1 || x == 2, x == 3:
+	switch x {
+	case 4:
+	case 1, 2, 3:
 	}
 
-	switch {
-	case x == 1 || x == 2, x == 3:
-	case x == 4:
+	switch x {
+	case 1, 2, 3:
+	case 4:
 	default:
 	}
 
-	switch {
-	case a == (x == y) || a == (x != y):
+	switch a {
+	case x == y, x != y:
 	}
 }
